{"id": "F06", "parts": ["Microplastic pollution, although ubiquitous, is not uniformly distributed over the planet.", "Areas with higher contamination concentrations have been identified such as the five oceanic gyres [26–29], the Arctic [9], the China Sea [30,31] and the Mediterranean Sea [24,30–32] and a very large number of microplastics have been collected in these areas."], "runs": {"release": {"key": "39d84acafe3d", "shown": [true, true], "warned": [false, false], "ms": 440, "status": "translated", "details": [], "error": null}, "previous": {"key": "39d84acafe3d", "shown": [true, false], "warned": [false, true], "ms": 531, "status": "partial", "details": [[], [{"code": "quantity", "severity": "severe", "detail": ""}, {"code": "direction", "severity": "severe", "detail": ""}, {"code": "fragmented-prose", "severity": "advisory"}]], "error": null}, "revised": {"key": "4ef36b248d54", "shown": [true, true], "warned": [false, false], "ms": 173, "status": "translated", "details": [[], []], "error": null}}}
{"id": "F07", "parts": ["Lakes may be especially contaminated because of long water retention times and proximity to pollution sources."], "runs": {"release": {"key": "af0b93a889d2", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 38, "status": "translated", "details": [], "error": null}, "previous": {"key": "af0b93a889d2", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 36, "status": "translated", "details": [[]], "error": null}, "revised": {"key": "af0b93a889d2", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 42, "status": "translated", "details": [[]], "error": null}}}
{"id": "F08", "parts": ["Filled circles are estimated means ± 95% CIs compiled from published studies for each environment with square denoting concentrations observed in this study."], "runs": {"release": {"key": "f8e1b19ea272", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 56, "status": "translated", "details": [], "error": null}, "previous": {"key": "f8e1b19ea272", "shown": [false], "warned": [true], "ms": 103, "status": "review", "details": [[{"code": "quantity", "severity": "severe", "detail": ""}]], "error": null}, "revised": {"key": "f8e1b19ea272", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 65, "status": "translated", "details": [[]], "error": null}}}
{"id": "F09", "parts": ["We found fewer microparticles in lakes from our field survey where resident microbial communities degraded organic matter more quickly (95% CI for effect: −0.50 to −0.14), as indicated by higher oxygen consumption rates in short-term laboratory incubations of lake water [56]."], "runs": {"release": {"key": "cff79649d9bb", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 237, "status": "translated", "details": [], "error": null}, "previous": {"key": "cff79649d9bb", "shown": [false], "warned": [true], "ms": 343, "status": "review", "details": [[{"code": "direction", "severity": "severe", "detail": ""}]], "error": null}, "revised": {"key": "75935b5e1a33", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 131, "status": "translated", "details": [[]], "error": null}}}
{"id": "F10", "parts": ["By contrast, we predicted lower concentrations in catchments with intact natural vegetation, such as forests [24], which can be less impacted by human activity."], "runs": {"release": {"key": "843b151ed1c4", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 60, "status": "translated", "details": [], "error": null}, "previous": {"key": "843b151ed1c4", "shown": [false], "warned": [true], "ms": 120, "status": "review", "details": [[{"code": "direction", "severity": "severe", "detail": ""}]], "error": null}, "revised": {"key": "843b151ed1c4", "shown": [true], "warned": [false], "ms": 63, "status": "translated", "details": [[]], "error": null}}}
